AB  - MobileSec is an open-source tool designed to perform static analysis of Android application packages. Various processes, such as APK preprocessing, cryptographic error identification, secret detection, and network configuration analysis, are included in this tool. A classifier called LightGBM is used to predict the category into which the problems detected during a scan should fall. The tool also includes a large language model, or LLM, feature that provides instructions on how to solve a given problem, depending on whether Java or Kotlin is used. Communication is handled through REST APIs and Kafka events. The results are stored in a MongoDB database. There is also a ReportGen feature that allows scanned data to be exported in PDF, JSON, and SARIF formats. A CI feature is also provided to automate the workflow. The tool was evaluated using the DroidBench and Ghera benchmarks. Moreover, it is modular, which means that changes can be made according to the needs of the user.
