AB  - VulnSight is a software framework for verifying whether known vulnerabilities are present in target software versions. Existing vulnerability databases and detection tools often rely on metadata or syntactic patch matching, which can fail under refactoring, file relocation, and long-term code evolution. Given a vulnerability description, patch, vulnerable and fixed reference snapshots, and a target version, VulnSight reconstructs two semantic abstractions, VulnPattern and SafePattern, identifies relevant target-side code regions, and performs LLM-guided semantic verification. The framework returns evidence-supported verdicts with interpretable reasoning. VulnSight provides language-aware preprocessing for Python, Java, and C/C++ projects, with systematic evaluations on Python and Java and preliminary case-based validation on C/C++.
